        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_RECORD",
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD",
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "You are generating Oracle widget payload.\n\nInputs:\n- kanbanCardDetails: {{$context.$variables.kanbanCardDetails}}\nCompute chart counts strictly from ToSupplyStatusMeaning in this array:\n- Empty count = rows where ToSupplyStatusMeaning == \"Empty\"\n- In Process count = rows where ToSupplyStatusMeaning == \"In process\"\nDo not use itemPullSequenceDetails for chart values.\nIf a category is absent, its count must be 0.\nThe table rows and chart totals must refer to the exact same rows.\nSchema requirements:\n\n1) Generate a chartWidget\n{\n  \"title\": \"Kanban Cards for <Item>\",\n  \"patternId\": \"chartWidget\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"type\": \"pie\",\n    \"data\": {\n      \"labels\": [\"Empty\",\"In Process\"],\n      \"datasets\": [\n        { \"data\": [emptyCount, inProcessCount], \"backgroundColor\": [\"#f44336\",\"#ff9800\"] }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n2) multiRecordWidget\nGenerate a multiRecordWidget with cols \n\"Number\"\t(KanbanCardNumber),\n\"Status\"\t(ToSupplyStatusMeaning) as Badge, (- Status MUST come only from `ToSupplyStatusMeaning` for that KanbanCardNumber)\n\"Point of Use\" (SubinventoryCode + '-' + (Locator if present, else SubinventoryCode only)),\n\"Source\" (SupplierName),\n\"Size\" (KanbanSize),\n\"Lead Time\" (ReplenishmentLeadTime) from {{$context.$variables. itemPullSequenceDetails}},\n\"Days Not Moved\" (cardStuckInStatusDuration.days ) from {{$context.$variables. itemPullSequenceDetails}}\norder the multiRecordWidget by supplierHoldTimeInMs in descending order.\nAdd a row-level action for each `multiRecordWidget` row.\nThen generate the row action as:\n{\n  \"title\": \"Update Pull Sequences - <item>\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"updates the number of kanban cards in pull sequences\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Change Status to Full\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"editSupplyStatus\\\", \\\"editSupplyStatus-<kanbancardId>-Full-\\\")\",\n  \"Prioritize\": false\n}\n\nReplace:\n- `<item>` with Item Number\n- `<kanbancardId>` with actual KanbanCardId from row data\n\nStrict Rules-:\n*Use only the data available in the provided array\n*Use the exact column names Don't add additional text\n*Do not infer, assume, or fabricate any values.\nFor every widget cell/action/title/summary value, output string only.\n- If value is null/undefined -> \"\"\n- If value is number/boolean -> convert to string\n- Never output object/array as a field value\n\n*If a field is missing in an object, leave the corresponding cell empty.\n\n*Do not add prefixes, suffixes, explanations, or extra text to any value.\n\n*Do not include any text outside of the table.\n\n*Do not reorder, rename, or modify column values.\n\n*If any of data is null or undefined show empty string"
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
